# Pinned public FastFlow SDK snapshot that PROVIDES HRX, built from source via
# `dev.py build hrx`. This is the public replacement for the private jtuyls/hrx
# prebuilt tarball pin in hrx-release.env.
#
# The SDK builds HRX from its projects/hrx submodule (github.com/ROCm/hrx-system)
# at the commit recorded in the SDK's own manifests/versions.toml [hrx].commit.
# provision-hrx-from-fastflow-sdk.sh checks out this ref, verifies the HRX
# submodule matches HRX_EXPECTED_COMMIT, runs `dev.py build hrx`, and stages the
# resulting build/hrx-install dev package into ./.hrx-release/ so the existing
# find_package(hrx CONFIG REQUIRED) flow (src/CMakeLists.txt) consumes it
# unchanged.
#
# NOTE: this moves JT's HRX from the older v2026.09.15 pin (c023c3e) up to
# v2026.10.13 (e53f2997), matching FLM_IRON. Shipped engine .so must be rebuilt
# against this HRX.

FASTFLOW_SDK_REPO="https://github.com/ROCm/FastFlow-SDK.git"
# Latest FastFlow SDK main carrying the HRX v2026.10.13 pin (PR #128). Pinned to
# a commit for reproducibility; HRX_EXPECTED_COMMIT below is the real contract.
FASTFLOW_SDK_REF="4af0efef2187fe3e9f878728ebecc03697c40986"

# Expected HRX (ROCm/hrx-system) commit at that SDK snapshot, i.e.
# flm-hrx-amdxdna-v2026.10.13 (-e53f299-). Verified after submodule checkout;
# the build aborts on drift.
HRX_EXPECTED_COMMIT="e53f2997faa23329621e69ed3024fe34eee30698"
